Here is a quick 'hangperson' program based on the ever-so-popular hangman game we used to relish playing as kids. I have forgottensome of the rules (in particular - how many wrong guesses you are allowed)so I just guessed on a couple of things.This was written on a system running SYSVR3. I make no guarantees thatit will run correctly anywhere. I do humbly apologize for someof the poor code, incoherent comments, and lack of a help screen but,what the hell, it was quick, easy, and now it's free. Please feel freeto hack it to death if you want.What you will have to do:    1. Unshar this file (which you may have done already)    2. edit main.c and change the define of WORDLIST to the path       of your ascii word list ( /usr/dict/words may be a good one ),       and change the define of NO_OF_WORDS to the total amount of       words in WORDLIST (`wc -l' might help there).    3. type makeenjoy!Thomas W. Necedaatt!homxb!amator       